,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,3838,374,279,6010,1948,279,3501,448,13934,400,4080,20,11,20,15087,323,4930,20,4999,20,15087,30,17399,697,4226,304,44548,17855,1352,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the distance between the points with coordinates $(-5,5)$ and $(5,-5)$? Express your answer in simplest radical form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"3d91e4b9ee96fbe54c1a3239f34561a1603cd54f18981ed55fd61be467859781"},"seconds":8.668019533157349,"seed":78734802598824791,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the distance between the points \\((-5, 5)\\) and \\((5, -5)\\), we use the distance formula. The distance formula between two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n\\]\n\nHere, the coordinates of the points are \\((-5, 5)\\) and \\((5, -5)\\). So, we substitute \\(x_1 = -5\\), \\(y_1 = 5\\), \\(x_2 = 5\\), and \\(y_2 = -5\\) into the formula:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(5 - (-5))^2 + (-5 - 5)^2}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expressions inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(5 + 5)^2 + (-5 - 5)^2} = \\sqrt{10^2 + (-10)^2}\n\\]\n\nCalculate the squares:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{100 + 100} = \\sqrt{200}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the square root:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{100 \\cdot 2} = \\sqrt{100} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} = 10\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the distance between the points \\((-5, 5)\\) and \\((5, -5)\\) is \\(\\boxed{10\\sqrt{2}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{10\\sqrt{2}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:405"}
